IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `roc-core`

-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021, current version as at 5 November 2026.
-- REGULATIVE RULES for the duties in Orders 46A, 52, 53, 54 and 55 that name a party who must act (and, for two, a time).
-- Source: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore Statutes Online.
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here has been checked against the official text.
--
-- WHAT THIS FILE IS FOR.  The decision functions in the `roc10-order-NN` modules answer "was the requirement met?" with
-- JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE / NOTHING.  A deontic rule answers a different question: what is still owed, by whom, and what
-- follows when a time passes.  Here each rule is a PARTY / MUST / WITHIN / HENCE / LEST chain run with #TRACE.
-- The brief does not let a deontic rule invent an actor, a time or a consequence the text does not give:
--   * where the text gives no time, the rule has no WITHIN (no time can run out);
--   * where the text gives no consequence of failure, LEST is the plain BREACH, and the reason names the provision;
--     what follows non-compliance is O 3 r 2(4), which is in another part's range, so no remedy is written here.
-- TIME.  A time in days is counted as O 3 r 3 counts it (lines 323 to 329): a deadline "within 14 days after" a date is
-- the date plus 14, inclusive; "at least 2 clear days before" a day is the day minus 3 (two days must intervene).
-- A #TRACE starts at day 0, the day of the event that starts the time, and an act AT n is on day n.
--
-- THE COURT'S POWER TO ORDER OTHERWISE.  O 46A r 2 opens "Unless the Court otherwise orders"; O 52 r 2(3) says "subject to any
-- directions given by the Court"; O 55 r 5 opens "Unless any order ... otherwise directs".  A deontic rule here cannot carry
-- that exception without inventing an actor and an event, so each rule below is the duty AS IT STANDS when the exception is
-- not engaged.  The decision functions (`o 46A r 2(b) the duty to serve a list and copies arises` and its companions) take the
-- exception as an input and answer JUST FALSE when it holds; the pairing is in roc10-tests-duties.l4.
-- A BREACH below records only that the time ran out.  What follows a missed time is O 3 r 2(4), in another part's range.
--
-- WHAT #TRACE DOES AND DOES NOT GIVE.  #ASSERT on a DEONTIC value is not supported by this binary (see NOTES.md,
-- "What the main binary does not accept").  So each #TRACE below has its outcome written beside it, read from the
-- output of `l4 run` on both main builds, and the same duty is asserted as a decision function in roc10-tests-duties.l4.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- O 46A r 2(b): a party who served a pleading before the action was placed on the Express Track must, within 14 days
-- after the date on which it was placed there, serve a list of and a copy of every document relied on.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
DECLARE `o 46A r 2(b) who acts` IS ONE OF
    `o 46A r 2(b) a party who served a pleading before the action was placed on the Express Track`

DECLARE `o 46A r 2(b) what is done` IS ONE OF
    `o 46A r 2(b) serve on every other party a list of and a copy of every document relied on`

-- src:6145 | ( b )
-- src:6146 | where any party to the action has served a pleading before the action was placed on the Express Track, that party must, within 14 days after the date on which the action is placed on the Express Track, serve on every other party a list of and a copy of every document relied on by that party to prove any allegation contained in that pleading. [S 504/2024 wef 01/07/2024]
@ref O 46A r 2(b) (src:6145-6146)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `o 46A r 2(b) who acts` `o 46A r 2(b) what is done`
DECIDE `o 46A r 2(b) the duty to serve the list and copies` IS
    PARTY `o 46A r 2(b) a party who served a pleading before the action was placed on the Express Track`
    MUST `o 46A r 2(b) serve on every other party a list of and a copy of every document relied on`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "O 46A r 2(b): the list and copies were not served within 14 days after the date on which the action was placed on the Express Track"

-- Served on day 14: in time (the 14th day after the date is inside "within 14 days after").
#TRACE `o 46A r 2(b) the duty to serve the list and copies` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 46A r 2(b) a party who served a pleading before the action was placed on the Express Track` DOES `o 46A r 2(b) serve on every other party a list of and a copy of every document relied on` AT 14
-- Outcome (read from l4 run, 1.6.109 and 1.6.108): FULFILLED.

-- Not served by day 15: the time has run out.
#TRACE `o 46A r 2(b) the duty to serve the list and copies` AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 15
-- Outcome (read from l4 run, 1.6.109 and 1.6.108): BREACH BY the party, with the reason text "O 46A r 2(b): the list and copies were not served within 14 days ...".

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- O 52 r 2(3): where the hearing is adjourned and the defendant was absent, the claimant must serve a written notice of
-- the adjourned hearing on the defendant at least 2 clear days before the day fixed for the hearing.
-- The day fixed is day 10 in these runs; the last day for service is day 7 (days 8 and 9 intervene).
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
DECLARE `o 52 r 2(3) who acts` IS ONE OF
    `o 52 r 2(3) the claimant`

DECLARE `o 52 r 2(3) what is done` IS ONE OF
    `o 52 r 2(3) serve a written notice of the adjourned hearing, with a copy of any further affidavit, on the defendant`

-- src:6502 | (3) Where the hearing is adjourned and the defendant was absent from the hearing, then, subject to any directions given by the Court, the claimant must serve a written notice of the adjourned hearing, together with a copy of any further affidavit intended to be used at that hearing, on the defendant at least 2 clear days before the day fixed for the hearing.
@ref O 52 r 2(3) (src:6502)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `o 52 r 2(3) who acts` `o 52 r 2(3) what is done`
DECIDE `o 52 r 2(3) the duty to serve the notice of the adjourned hearing` IS
    PARTY `o 52 r 2(3) the claimant`
    MUST `o 52 r 2(3) serve a written notice of the adjourned hearing, with a copy of any further affidavit, on the defendant`
    WITHIN 7
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "O 52 r 2(3): the notice of the adjourned hearing was not served at least 2 clear days before the day fixed for the hearing"

#TRACE `o 52 r 2(3) the duty to serve the notice of the adjourned hearing` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 52 r 2(3) the claimant` DOES `o 52 r 2(3) serve a written notice of the adjourned hearing, with a copy of any further affidavit, on the defendant` AT 7
-- Outcome (read from l4 run, 1.6.109 and 1.6.108): FULFILLED.

#TRACE `o 52 r 2(3) the duty to serve the notice of the adjourned hearing` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 52 r 2(3) the claimant` DOES `o 52 r 2(3) serve a written notice of the adjourned hearing, with a copy of any further affidavit, on the defendant` AT 8
-- Outcome (read from l4 run, 1.6.109 and 1.6.108): BREACH BY the claimant (served on day 8, only day 9 intervenes before the day fixed: one clear day, not two).

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- O 53 r 21(3) and (4): after service of foreign process (or a failed attempt) the authorised officer or process server
-- must make an affidavit; after it is tendered the Registrar must issue the certificate or the statement to the
-- Attorney-General.  The text fixes no time for either, so neither has a WITHIN.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
DECLARE `o 53 r 21 who acts` IS ONE OF
    `o 53 r 21(3) the authorised officer or process server`
    `o 53 r 21(4) the Registrar`

DECLARE `o 53 r 21 what is done` IS ONE OF
    `o 53 r 21(3) make an affidavit of service or attempted service`
    `o 53 r 21(4) issue to the Attorney-General the certificate or the statement`

-- src:6681 | (3) After the service of any process under section 38 has been effected or (as the case may be) attempts to effect service of it have failed, the authorised officer or process server (as the case may be) must make an affidavit of service or attempted service, which — ( a )
-- src:6682 | describes when, where and how the authorised officer or process server (as the case may be) did or attempted to effect service of the process; and
-- src:6683 | ( b )
-- src:6684 | exhibits a copy of the process received with the request for service.
-- src:6685 | (4) After the affidavit is tendered to the Registrar, the Registrar must issue to the Attorney‑General either the certificate or the statement referred to in paragraphs (5) and (6).
@ref O 53 r 21(3); O 53 r 21(4) (src:6681-6685)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `o 53 r 21 who acts` `o 53 r 21 what is done`
DECIDE `o 53 r 21 the duties after service of foreign process` IS
    PARTY `o 53 r 21(3) the authorised officer or process server`
    MUST `o 53 r 21(3) make an affidavit of service or attempted service`
    HENCE (
        PARTY `o 53 r 21(4) the Registrar`
        MUST `o 53 r 21(4) issue to the Attorney-General the certificate or the statement`
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BECAUSE "O 53 r 21(4): the Registrar did not issue the certificate or the statement to the Attorney-General")
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "O 53 r 21(3): the authorised officer or process server did not make an affidavit of service or attempted service"

#TRACE `o 53 r 21 the duties after service of foreign process` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 53 r 21(3) the authorised officer or process server` DOES `o 53 r 21(3) make an affidavit of service or attempted service` AT 3
    PARTY `o 53 r 21(4) the Registrar` DOES `o 53 r 21(4) issue to the Attorney-General the certificate or the statement` AT 6
-- Outcome (read from l4 run, 1.6.109 and 1.6.108): FULFILLED.

#TRACE `o 53 r 21 the duties after service of foreign process` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 53 r 21(3) the authorised officer or process server` DOES `o 53 r 21(3) make an affidavit of service or attempted service` AT 3
-- Outcome (read from l4 run, 1.6.109 and 1.6.108): the residual obligation: the Registrar must still issue the certificate or the statement.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- O 55 r 5: the examiner must send the deposition to the Registrar, and the Registrar must (a) give a certificate and
-- (b) send it with the documents annexed to the Permanent Secretary to the Minister (or to the other person under a
-- Civil Procedure Convention).  No time is fixed.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
DECLARE `o 55 r 5 who acts` IS ONE OF
    `o 55 r 5 the examiner`
    `o 55 r 5 the Registrar`

DECLARE `o 55 r 5 what is done` IS ONE OF
    `o 55 r 5 send the deposition to the Registrar`
    `o 55 r 5(a) give a certificate sealed with the seal of the Supreme Court`
    `o 55 r 5(b) send the certificate with the documents annexed`

-- src:6718 | 5. Unless any order made in pursuance of this Order for the examination of any witness otherwise directs, the examiner before whom the examination was taken must send the deposition of that witness to the Registrar, and the Registrar must — ( a )
-- src:6719 | give a certificate sealed with the seal of the Supreme Court for use out of the jurisdiction identifying the documents annexed to the certificate, that is to say, the letter of request, certificate, or other document from the court or tribunal out of the jurisdiction requesting the examination, the order of the Court for examination and the deposition taken in pursuance of the order; and
-- src:6720 | ( b )
-- src:6721 | send the certificate with the documents annexed thereto to the Permanent Secretary to the Minister, or, where the letter of request, certificate or other document was sent to the Registrar by some other person in accordance with a Civil Procedure Convention, to that other person, for transmission to that court or tribunal.
@ref O 55 r 5 (src:6718-6721)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `o 55 r 5 who acts` `o 55 r 5 what is done`
DECIDE `o 55 r 5 the duties as to the deposition` IS
    PARTY `o 55 r 5 the examiner`
    MUST `o 55 r 5 send the deposition to the Registrar`
    HENCE (
        PARTY `o 55 r 5 the Registrar`
        MUST `o 55 r 5(a) give a certificate sealed with the seal of the Supreme Court`
        HENCE (
            PARTY `o 55 r 5 the Registrar`
            MUST `o 55 r 5(b) send the certificate with the documents annexed`
            HENCE FULFILLED
            LEST BREACH BECAUSE "O 55 r 5(b): the Registrar did not send the certificate with the documents annexed")
        LEST BREACH BECAUSE "O 55 r 5(a): the Registrar did not give the certificate")
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "O 55 r 5: the examiner did not send the deposition to the Registrar"

#TRACE `o 55 r 5 the duties as to the deposition` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 55 r 5 the examiner` DOES `o 55 r 5 send the deposition to the Registrar` AT 1
    PARTY `o 55 r 5 the Registrar` DOES `o 55 r 5(a) give a certificate sealed with the seal of the Supreme Court` AT 2
    PARTY `o 55 r 5 the Registrar` DOES `o 55 r 5(b) send the certificate with the documents annexed` AT 3
-- Outcome (read from l4 run, 1.6.109 and 1.6.108): FULFILLED.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- O 54 r 2(3): the officer must administer the oath in the form and manner set out in paragraph (2).  No time is fixed.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
DECLARE `o 54 r 2(3) who acts` IS ONE OF
    `o 54 r 2(3) the officer`

DECLARE `o 54 r 2(3) what is done` IS ONE OF
    `o 54 r 2(3) administer the oath in the form and manner set out in paragraph (2)`

-- src:6694 | (3) The officer must (unless the person about to take the oath is permitted under the Act to do otherwise, or is physically incapable of so taking the oath) administer the oath in the form and manner set out in paragraph (2).
@ref O 54 r 2(3) (src:6694)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `o 54 r 2(3) who acts` `o 54 r 2(3) what is done`
DECIDE `o 54 r 2(3) the duty to administer the oath` IS
    PARTY `o 54 r 2(3) the officer`
    MUST `o 54 r 2(3) administer the oath in the form and manner set out in paragraph (2)`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "O 54 r 2(3): the officer did not administer the oath in the form and manner set out in paragraph (2)"

#TRACE `o 54 r 2(3) the duty to administer the oath` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 54 r 2(3) the officer` DOES `o 54 r 2(3) administer the oath in the form and manner set out in paragraph (2)` AT 0
-- Outcome (read from l4 run, 1.6.109 and 1.6.108): FULFILLED.
